  "notes": "The datasheet's interface block is explicit and unusual: '**2x 10/100/1000M Ethernet**' WAN and '**9x 10/100/1000M Ethernet**' LAN. Nine LAN ports is the number to keep - not eight, and not ten: a lab that rounds it to a typical 8-port switch side will be short by one cable, so the test pins 9. The embedded LTE-A Pro modem has redundant SIM slots again (one modem, one `wwan0`), and the two USB sockets are WAN-capable but are not Ethernet, so they are described here rather than modelled as ports. Router throughput 2.5 Gbps and PepVPN 500 Mbps with 256-bit AES are quoted; power is 30 W max from 12-30 V DC with no PoE in or out, hence `poeIn: 0` on every copper port. Unlike the AP One range, this model does document a **Command Line Interface**, so `cli` is declared."
